WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.300
-We're hanging out with our
good pal, Matthew McConaughey,

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.300
who stars in the new film
"Sing 2."

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.300
What a cast in "Sing 2."
-Isn't it?

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.701
-Well, it's just you,
Scarlett Johansson,

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.801
Reese Witherspoon,
and then -- no big deal --

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:16.400
you add Bono to the mix.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.434
-Bono shows up.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:18.834
-Yeah, no big deal.
-Thank you, Bono.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.701
-It's always
a party when Bono shows up.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.467
-It is always a party
when Bono shows up.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:27.000
-Yeah. I mean, it's an amazing
part of the movie, as well.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.834
I loved the first "Sing."

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.200
My kids loved it, as well.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.300
But "Sing 2," another hopeful
movie, makes you laugh.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.200
It makes you want to
sing, obviously.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.767
But the stakes are
higher in this one.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:39.968
-Stakes are higher in this one.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:43.000
We pulled off the show in
"Sing 1" in our town.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.934
Now we're taking it to
Redshore City,

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:49.367
which is, in our movie, Vegas,
the biggest stage on the planet.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.501
And -- whew! --
are we going to pull it off?

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:52.767
How can we pull it off?

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:55.167
I, as Buster Moon,
who's got to put the show on,

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:58.234
write a lot of checks
that I can't cash,

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.400
make a lot of promises
I don't know if I can keep.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.901
But with the help of a lot of
my team in the show --

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.901
You go see it,
see if we pulled it off.

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.067
-It's so cute. It's so funny.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.501
-The movie is -- it's good news.

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:11.567
We need some good news
right now.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:12.634
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.234
-Exactly right.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:17.067
-It's about chasing the dream
but also, how do you get it?

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.501
The hustle you got to have,
the dealing with the rejection,

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:21.400
which is part of it,
all the doubt,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.033
but can you believe your way
through the doubt?

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.501
-Yep.
-You know? And it's fun.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:26.634
There's something
for everyone to sing.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.367
-It's your kids.
You're the parents.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.400
It's your grandparents.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.767
You can all sing along
in this one.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.067
-By the way,
the soundtrack on this one --

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.667
I don't know how you
pulled it off.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.801
Are we allowed to even say
the names or we don't know?

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.033
-I think we can.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:41.167
-Can we say BTS, Prince,
Cardi B.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.934
-Yeah.
-And, obviously, U2.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.067
-Yeah. New song.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.033
U2 has got a new song you
never heard before

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.767
and the classics off of
"Joshua Tree."

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.834
-I mean --
-No, no, no, it's thick.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.033
It is thick.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.968
-I remember,
I was walking around New York,

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.567
and I got one of those --

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.067
This is back when
I was on "SNL."

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:01.834
I got just a radio, just, like,
a Sony radio, like, a Walkman.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:03.400
No tape,
just to listen to radio,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.100
because when you are in
New York, you just walk around.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.100
There's no -- And, you know,
I just want to listen to music.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.434
And "Where the Streets
Have No Name" came on,

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:11.901
and I just go --
And it was like,

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.167
"I want to run."

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.234
And I just started running.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.601
I just ran until
I hit the water.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:18.334
Yeah. I just loved it.

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:19.701
I go -- It just felt right.

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.601
I go, "That's what Bono
would want me to do."

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:22.601
He'd want me to just
take off -- right? --

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.734
and keep running, man.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.100
-That's exactly what
he wanted you to do.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.567
-Exactly what -- And I did it.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.701
Then I had to walk all the way
back with a different song.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.934
I can't control the radio.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.200
I know your daughter got to do
a little part in this film.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.501
-She did.
-That's so cute.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.767
-Vida got a couple of lines
in "Sing 2."

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.000
She plays a piglet who
is scuba-diving in chocolate.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.067
-Yeah! Come on!

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:43.367
-Saying, "This is
the best day of my life."

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.434
-I mean, it is the best day if

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:45.701
you get to scuba-dive
in chocolate.

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:48.400
-How about that?
-I mean, it's the most fun.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.334
And I got to tell everybody.
It's just so -- And Nick Kroll.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.300
-Nick Kroll.
"I'm fine. How are you?"

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.434
-Gunter, I mean --
-Gunter, oh!

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:57.501
-Anyways, it's great.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:58.701
The whole family
should go check it out.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:02:59.868
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.100
Here's Matthew McConaughey
in "Sing 2."

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.434
Take a look at this.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.267
-Miss Crawly, it's me, Mr. Moon.

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:06.667
I haven't heard from you
in a while.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.434
I'm starting to worry here.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.567
-Moon!
-[ Gasps ]

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.367
-Mr. Crystal.

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.934
-Your set designs
are a disgrace!

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.267
-What?!

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.901
♪♪

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.400
-[ Laughs ]
I'm just messing with you.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.000
Where is your
sense of humor, huh?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.801
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.934
-Anyway, this is
my daughter, Porsha.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.300
-Hey!

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.767
-Nice to meet you, Porsha.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.734
-She wants to meet Calloway.
Big fan, aren't you, baby?

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:30.868
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:32.667
I'm, like,
so into vintage right now.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.033
-So, where is he?

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:38.901
-Uh, well, I'm -- I'm not
expecting Clay on set just yet.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:39.934
I mean --
-Wait.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.601
Is this like a sky-fi show?

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.234
-Uh, sci-fi?

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.200
Yes. Yes, it is.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.801
I love sky-fi.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.000
-Oh, it's a "ski-fi."

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.200
-I love "ski-fi," too!
-I love "ski-fi," too!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.801
Matthew McConaughey, everybody!

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:57.634
"Sing 2" opens in theaters
December 22nd.

